config SIMAAI_MLA
	tristate "SiMa.ai Modalix MLA (Machine Learning Accelerator) driver"
	depends on ARM64 || COMPILE_TEST
	depends on IO_URING
	depends on DMA_SHARED_BUFFER
	depends on DMABUF_HEAPS
	select DMA_CMA
	help
	  Support for the SiMa.ai Modalix Machine Learning Accelerator.
	  Exposes /dev/mla, an io_uring_cmd based interface for loading and
	  executing compiled MLA models. Userspace runtime is mla-rt /
	  libMLArt.so from the sibling mla_rt repository.

	  DRAM buffers prefer the shared simaai,mla fallback DMA heap when
	  available, otherwise the heap over the node's memory-region.
	  Enable DMABUF_HEAPS_CARVEOUT for the legacy reserved pool, or
	  DMABUF_HEAPS_CMA for reusable DMS and the shared fallback heap.

	  To compile as a module, choose M here: the module will be called
	  mla.
